# AArch64 shape_refuse + no_output audit (Phase 3 of the 9-phase 11/10 plan)

File: openOODA/audit/aarch64-shape-refuse-gate.oot

Logline: Records the AArch64 shape refusal pre-check and the no_output runtime stub port that closes 3 of the 5 known silent-miscompile shapes.

Setup: Re-reads oodac/aarch64_emit_shape_refuse.oo, oodac/aarch64_emit_no_output.oo, oodac/aarch64_emit.oo, and the 5 fixtures in fixtures/.

Beats:
  1. oodac/aarch64_emit_shape_refuse.oo is a straight AAPCS64 port of oodac/x86_emit_shape_refuse.oo (token helpers swapped x86_tok_k -> a64_tok_k).
  2. oodac/aarch64_emit_no_output.oo is a straight AAPCS64 port of oodac/x86_emit_no_output.oo (frame helpers swapped x86_emit_frame_* -> aarch64_emit_frame_*; literals via adrp/add instead of %rip-relative; syscalls 64/93 retained).
  3. aarch64_emit.oo wires the gate between the if-test and the 25-arm dispatch ladder. ERR lines are printed and process_exit(1) is called.

== Fixed bugs during the port ==

* The 3-arm match signature loop exited on the first RBRACE it saw, not on the match's closing RBRACE. The x86 version has the same bug. AArch64 port fixes it: track depth, break on RBRACE-at-depth-0 only.
* The struct signature was originally DOT-token-only; in real Oo source the DOT appears in file paths (`aarch64_emit.oo`), method calls (`sh_realpath(p, ".")`), and shell commands (`wc -l`). The port narrows to KW_TYPE or `struct` IDENT only. This is more restrictive than x86 but is the only way to avoid false positives without a real parser.

== Gate behavior ==

Tested against the 5 fixtures:

* aarch64_shape_float_refuse.oo (Float runtime, no const-fold) -> ERR Float usage (refused)
* aarch64_shape_match_refuse.oo (3-arm match on Int, no Some/Ok) -> ERR 3-arm match (refused)
* aarch64_shape_list_refuse.oo (List declared, no list op) -> ERR List[T] (refused)
* aarch64_shape_float_pass.oo (let x: Float = 3.14; println(x)) -> emits Float const-fold floor (passes)
* aarch64_list_int.oo (pre-existing List runtime) -> emits List runtime floor, runs on qemu-aarch64, prints 342 (passes)

Three of the five shapes (Float, 3-arm match, List) are now refused-don't-miscompiled at the gate. The Result[T] shape is allowed if the source uses the tagged-union match path; the struct shape is allowed if the source uses `type` or `struct NAME { ... }`. The struct-matcher's own DOT+IDENT trigger in aarch64_match_struct remains a known pre-existing issue (qemu_runtime_smoke trips it; out of scope for this phase).

== Tag and version ==

Tag v0.225.33 on commit (Phase 3 commit). ooda.pkg version=0.225.33.

== Remaining gap ==

Phase 4 (AST-path runtime smoke), Phase 5 (AST-path runtime), Phase 6 (AAPCS64 multi-function-call), Phase 7 (cross-arch output equivalence), Phase 8 (match/closure fixtures), Phase 9 (Tier 1 wiring) still pending. The no_output runtime is compiled but not yet integrated; that belongs to a future "runtime-blob tail" change in aarch64_emit.oo.
